---

Provenance: this project began as a structural and conceptual cousin of
blader/humanizer (https://github.com/blader/humanizer), also MIT licensed,
which built its original AI-writing-tell taxonomy on Wikipedia's "Signs of AI
writing" guide (WikiProject AI Cleanup). Credit to Blader for that original
taxonomy and the draft-audit-rewrite process this skill still follows. This
repository is an independent rewrite, not a fork: its pattern list, wording,
and version history are maintained on their own schedule and do not track
blader/humanizer's.

Some later pattern material (structural rhythm and parataxis rules, the
extended high-frequency vocabulary set, and the plain-text formatting rules)
draws on jalaalrd/anti-ai-slop-writing
(https://github.com/jalaalrd/anti-ai-slop-writing), also MIT licensed. That
material was rewritten rather than copied, and recalibrated from its
hard banned-word framing to this project's cluster-based judgment. As with
blader/humanizer, this repository does not track that project's releases.
